    {
      "id": "5b3e1a2c-0000-4d6e-9f70-8a1b2c3d4e5f",
      "name": "About this workflow",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -60,
        -980
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 760,
        "height": 760,
        "content": "## Translate and dub a video into several languages\n\nOne video link in, a dubbed copy for every language you list out. Each copy has a new voice saying the translated lines at the time the original was said, with the line as a caption.\n\n**Self-hosted n8n only for now:** it saves the MP4s on disk. On n8n Cloud, save them to Google Drive instead.\n\n### How it works\n1. Shotstack's Ingest API transcribes the video into timed captions.\n2. Claude translates every caption into each language, short enough to say in the same time.\n3. **Check the translation** sends anything that doesn't line up back to Claude.\n4. One Shotstack render per language: the original video muted, an ElevenLabs voice saying each line on time, and captions.\n\n### Setup steps\n1. Add an Anthropic API key to **Claude** and **Claude (fixes)**.\n2. Add a Shotstack API key to **Transcribe the video**, **Check the transcript**, **Make the video** and **Check the render**. Free trial: https://shotstack.io/?utm_source=n8n&utm_medium=template&utm_campaign=translate&utm_content=workflow_note\n3. Make an empty `translated` folder in n8n's files folder (`/home/node/.n8n-files` in Docker). On an npm install, change that path in **Save the video**.\n4. Put your video link and languages in **Your video**, then click **Execute workflow**.\n\n### Good to know\n- The voice costs 0.3 Shotstack credits per 1,000 characters, and renders are billed by the second, so a short clip costs well under a credit per language plus the transcription.\n- Any of ElevenLabs Multilingual's 29 languages works. Change the voice or how loud the original stays in **Your video**."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "5b3e1a2c-0040-4d6e-9f70-8a1b2c3d4e5f",
      "name": "Section: transcribe",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
